# Everything in this directory is served as a static asset by Cloudflare Workers,
# because `wrangler.toml` points `[assets] directory` straight at the package root.
# These entries are development-only and nothing on the site asks for them:
# verified with `grep -rn "package.json\|test/pure\|test/render"` across app.js,
# index.html, i18n.js, style.css and packages/server/src — no hits.
#
# `src/` is deliberately NOT listed. app.js imports ./src/geom.js and
# ./src/format.js at runtime, so those files are part of the shipped bundle, not
# a leak; excluding them would break the first paint.
#
# Wrangler drops `.assetsignore`, `_headers` and `_redirects` from the upload on
# its own. To see the decisions, run `wrangler deploy --dry-run --log-level=debug`
# and look for lines reading "Ignoring asset:".
/test/
package.json
